## Impact

The `DepositTokenLibrary::withdrawUnderlyingCollateralToken` and `DepositTokenLibrary::withdrawUnderlyingTokenFromVariablePool` functions are external and anyone can call them with arbitrary input arguments. That means a malicious user can set arbitrary address for `from` parameter and his/her address for `to` address. In that way a malicious user can withdraw funds that are not intended to withdraw. 
