# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When a debt position is repaid, lenders can claim their borrow tokens with interest using the claim function. The claimAmount is calculated as follows.

(From docs : https://docs.size.credit/technical-docs/contracts/3.6-claim)

```solidity
uint256 claimAmount = Math.mulDivDown(
            creditPosition.credit, state.data.borrowAToken.liquidityIndex(), debtPosition.liquidityIndexAtRepayment
        );
```

It uses a token's current liquidity index and the liquidity index when repayment has been made. The problem is that if a lender wants to claim his tokens after repayment, the current liquidity index and the liquidityIndexAtRepayment will be the same, and thus, the lender won't get any interest.

```solidity
function executeRepay(State storage state, RepayParams calldata params) external {
        DebtPosition storage debtPosition = state.getDebtPosition(params.debtPositionId);

        state.data.borrowAToken.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), debtPosition.futureValue);
        debtPosition.liquidityIndexAtRepayment = state.data.borrowAToken.liquidityIndex(); //@audit !!
        state.repayDebt(params.debtPositionId, debtPosition.futureValue);

        emit Events.Repay(params.debtPositionId);
    }
```


If the protocol wants to give interest that comes from AAVE to lenders, it should at least use position creation time instead of the liquidityIndexAtRepayment to give interest to lenders correctly.

