# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There are different variations of liquidations in Size, the standard liquidation via `liquidate()`, the self liquidation via `selfLiqiuidate()` and the [liquidateWithReplacement()](https://docs.size.credit/technical-docs/contracts/3.5-liquidations#id-3.5.3.3-liquidation-with-replacement) whcih liquidates a loan and immediately reassigns the retrieved value to another loan/ borrow offer. 

So we can say `liquidateWithReplacement()` is a combination of` liquidate()` + `buyCreditMarket()` (this is used to fill borrow orders). 

The size protocol has several global limits which are enforced through the system to limit user behaviour and are stored as riskConfigs. I will focus on  `state.riskConfig.minimumCreditBorrowAToken` here. `riskConfig.minimumCreditBorrowAToken` is a global limit which specifies the [minumum amount that can be borrowed as a loan](https://docs.size.credit/technical-docs/governance-variables-and-fees#protocol-safety-parameters). `liquidateWithReplacement()` liquidates a loan and then fills another borrowOffer/ loan,  but does not check that the amount given as loan is not lower than `state.riskConfig.minimumCreditBorrowAToken`.  Do note that  `buyCreditMarket()` validates this as seen [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/8850e25fb088898e9cf86f9be1c401ad155bea86/src/libraries/actions/BuyCreditMarket.sol#L90C1-L93C10). This ensures that the borrowAtoken amount that is transferred to the borrower is not lower than the `riskConfig.minimumCreditBorrowAToken`. Snippets from `buyCreditMarket()` below showing the transfer. 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-size/blob/8850e25fb088898e9cf86f9be1c401ad155bea86/src/libraries/actions/BuyCreditMarket.sol#L157
```solidity
